# Reflection – Project Time Management

### Why is identifying the critical path important for project managers?
Identifying the critical path is important because it shows which activities directly affect the project completion date. Any delay in these activities will delay the entire project, so they require close monitoring.

### Which activity posed the highest scheduling risk?
Model Training and Tuning posed the highest scheduling risk because it depends on data quality, system resources, and multiple iterations to achieve the required accuracy.

### What trade-offs are involved when crashing a project?
Crashing a project reduces the overall duration but increases costs and resource usage. It may also increase workload pressure and risk of errors.
